##DESCRIPTION
##  Statistics problem: confidence intervals
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Hypothesis tests)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Date(7/13/2012)
## Institution(UBC)
## Author(Djun Kim)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('statistics', 'statistical inference', 'hypothesis test', 'p-value', 'interpretatin')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserCheckboxList.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");

$cb = CheckboxList(
    [ [
        'The chance of committing a Type I error changes from 0.10 to 0.05.',

        'The test becomes more stringent to reject the null hypothesis (i.e., '
            . 'it becomes harder to reject the null hypothesis).',
        'The chance that the null hypothesis is true changes from 0.10 to 0.05.',
        'The chance of committing a Type II error changes from 0.10 to 0.05.',
        'The test becomes less stringent to reject the null hypothesis (i.e. it '
            . 'becomes easier to reject the null hypothesis).',
        'It becomes easier to prove that the null hypothesis is true.',
        'It becomes harder to prove that the null hypothesis is true.'
    ] ],
    [ 0, 1 ],
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML

When one changes the significance level of a hypothesis test from 0.10 to 0.05, which of the following will happen? Check all that apply.

[_]{$cb}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The only statements that are true are: [$cb]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT(); 